/-!
# Upper shriek of a complete intersection homomorphism

Let `φ : R → A` be a local complete intersection homomorphism.  Such a
homomorphism is perfect, so algebraic upper shriek is derived tensor product over `R` with the
relative dualizing complex `ω_{A/R} = φ^!(R)`:  `φ^!(K) = K ⊗_R^L ω_{A/R}` for every `K` in
`D(R)`, naturally in `K`.  When the kernel of a presentation `P = R[x_1, …, x_n] ↠ A` is
generated by a weakly regular sequence of length `c`, the relative dualizing complex is the free
module of rank one in degree `c - n`, so it is an invertible object of `D(A)`.  For a local
complete intersection — the kernel of a presentation Koszul-regular rather than generated by a
regular sequence — the relative dualizing complex is still invertible, being a shifted copy of
the ring after one principal localization at each prime.

## Main results

* `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.upperShriekFunctor_iso_derivedTensorProduct_of_lci` —
  the tensor formula of [Stacks, Tag 0E4B].
* `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.nonempty_upperShriekFunctor_obj_unit_iso_single`:
  the relative dualizing complex of such a presentation is the free module of rank one in degree
  `c - n`.
* `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.isInvertible_upperShriekFunctor_obj_unit_of_isWeaklyRegular` —
  invertibility of the relative dualizing complex, [Stacks, Tag 0E4B] for a presentation whose
  kernel is generated by a weakly regular sequence.
* `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.isInvertible_upperShriekFunctor_obj_unit_of_isKoszulRegular` —
  invertibility of the relative dualizing complex, [Stacks, Tag 0E4B] for a presentation of a
  homomorphism from a Noetherian ring whose kernel is a Koszul-regular ideal.
* `isInvertible_upperShriekFunctor_obj_unit_of_isLocalCompleteIntersection`, in the same
  namespace — the same for a local complete intersection homomorphism and an arbitrary
  presentation of it.

## Implementation notes

The relative dualizing complex is the value of the upper shriek functor of a polynomial
presentation at `R`, as in `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.UpperShriek.Defs`; no choice of
presentation is made, so both statements are the ones for an arbitrary presentation, and the
object they speak about is the same one, the upper shriek of the presentation at the unit of
`D(R)`.

Perfectness of a local complete intersection homomorphism is [Stacks, Tag 07EN]
(`RingHom.IsLocalCompleteIntersection.perfect`); [Stacks, Tag 068Y] at the presentation
(`Algebra.Perfect.exists_finite_projective_resolution`, read through [Stacks, Tag 066Q]) makes `A`
a perfect module over its polynomial algebra, and the tensor formula for a perfect homomorphism is
[Stacks, Tag 0BZU].  The latter carries the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0BZE] for the surjection
of the presentation as an explicit hypothesis, which the library does not prove; it is passed
along here unchanged.

Invertibility is proved by computing the complex, not by a local criterion: the upper shriek of
a presentation is `RHom_P(A, - ⊗_R^L P)[n]`, and `RHom_P(A, P)` is `A` in degree `c` because the
quotient by each element of the sequence has kernel free of rank one, where derived Hom from the
quotient is the shift by `-1` of derived base change ([Stacks, Tag 0BZH] computes it as the
single complex on the inverse of the conormal module, which is free of rank one here), and
derived Hom composes along the resulting chain by [Stacks, Tag 0C0F].  A free module of rank one
in a fixed degree is locally a shifted unit on the whole spectrum, hence invertible by
[Stacks, Tag 0FNT].

The local complete intersection condition gives such a sequence only after localizing on the
polynomial algebra, so the local case is proved by the local criterion of [Stacks, Tag 0FNT]
instead: at a prime `𝔮` of `A` the kernel becomes, after one principal localization `P → P_g`,
generated by a regular sequence, and
`Dualizing.LocalCompleteIntersection.nonempty_iso_single_away` transports the resulting
computation of `RHom_{P_g}(A_{φ(g)}, P_g)` back to the derived localization of `RHom_P(A, P)` at
`φ(g)`.  That transport replaces the isomorphism assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0BZN] at the flat map
`P → P_g`, which this library proves only modulo `Dualizing.KFlatAlgebraActionEq`: it compares the
two objects degreewise, through `Ext` over `P`, where the base-change isomorphism of
[Stacks, Tag 0A6A] is available unconditionally.  That it loses naturality does not matter, since
only the value at the unit is needed.

Koszul-regularity of the kernel of one presentation gives it for every presentation, by
[Stacks, Tag 07CZ], so the statement for a local complete intersection homomorphism holds at an
arbitrary presentation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E4B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E4B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BZU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BZU)
